            {
                "name": "CVE-2023-5752",
                "score": 4,
                "severity": "Medium",
                "vectors": "",
                "description": "Command Injection in pip when used with Mercurial\nWhen installing a package from a Mercurial VCS URL, e.g. `pip install hg+...`, with pip prior to v23.3, the specified Mercurial revision could be used to inject arbitrary configuration options to the `hg clone` call (e.g. `--config`). Controlling the Mercurial configuration can modify how and which repository is installed. This vulnerability does not affect users who aren't installing from Mercurial.\n",
                "file_name": "usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/pip-21.2.4",
                "package_name": "python:pip",
                "package_version": "21.2.4",
                "fixed_version": "23.3",
